.TH GRIDDYCTL 1 "2026-05-23" "GriddyWM 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
griddyctl \- Control interface for the GriddyWM Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B griddyctl
[\fB\-j\fR]
[\fB\-\-batch\fR \fIcmds\fR]
\fIcommand\fR
[\fIarguments\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B griddyctl
communicates with a running
.BR griddy (1)
compositor via its UNIX command socket.
It can query compositor state, dispatch window management actions, reload
configuration, and subscribe to live event streams.
.PP
The socket path is determined from the
.B GRIDDY_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
environment variable (e.g.\&
.IR griddy_1234 ),
which
.B griddy
exports automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-j
Output JSON instead of the default plain-text format.
.TP
.BI \-\-batch " cmds"
Send multiple commands in a single round trip.
Commands are separated by
.BR " ; "
(space-semicolon-space).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS dispatch
.TP
.BI dispatch " action " [ args... ]
Execute a window management action.
.PP
.B Workspace navigation:
.RS
.TP
.B workspace-left, workspace-right, workspace-up, workspace-down
Move focus to the adjacent workspace in the given direction.
.TP
.BI workspace " col,row"
Jump to the workspace at grid coordinates
.IR col , row
(zero-based).
.TP
.B workspace-prev, workspace-next
Move to the previous/next workspace in history.
.RE
.PP
.B Window focus:
.RS
.TP
.B focus-left, focus-right, focus-up, focus-down
Move keyboard focus to the adjacent slot.
.TP
.B focus-cycle, focus-cycle-back
Cycle focus through windows on the current workspace.
.RE
.PP
.B Window placement:
.RS
.TP
.B slot-half-left, slot-half-right
Tile the focused window in the left/right half.
.TP
.B slot-quarter-tl, slot-quarter-tr, slot-quarter-bl, slot-quarter-br
Tile in a quarter-screen slot (top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right).
.TP
.B state-fullscreen-toggle
Toggle fullscreen state.
.TP
.B state-total-fullscreen-toggle
Toggle total-fullscreen (covers layer-shell panels).
.TP
.B state-floating-toggle
Toggle floating state.
.TP
.B state-minimise-toggle
Toggle minimized state.
.RE
.PP
.B Window movement:
.RS
.TP
.BI move-window-to " col,row"
Move the focused window to workspace at
.IR col , row .
.RE
.PP
.B Window control:
.RS
.TP
.B kill-window
Close the focused window (graceful send_close).
.TP
.B pin-toggle
Toggle whether the window appears on all workspaces.
.TP
.B urgent-toggle
Toggle the urgent flag on the focused window.
.RE
.PP
.B Overview and minimap:
.RS
.TP
.B overview-toggle
Enter or exit overview mode.
.TP
.B minimap-toggle
Toggle the minimap HUD.
.RE
.PP
.B Submaps:
.RS
.TP
.BI submap " name"
Enter a named key-submap (modal mode).
.TP
.B submap-reset
Exit the active submap.
.RE
.PP
.B Compositor control:
.RS
.TP
.BI exec " command"
Run a shell command.
.TP
.B lock
Activate the screen lock.
.TP
.B quit
Exit the compositor.
.RE
.SS get
.TP
.B get workspaces
List all workspaces and their properties.
.TP
.B get windows
List all managed windows.
.TP
.B get activewindow
Show the currently focused window.
.TP
.B get activeworkspace
Show the currently focused workspace.
.TP
.B get grid
Show the full grid state.
.TP
.B get monitors
List connected outputs and their properties.
.TP
.B get version
Show compositor version information.
.TP
.B get layers
List active layer-shell surfaces (bars, overlays, backgrounds).
.TP
.B get shaders
Show the active screen post-process shader.
.TP
.B get cursorpos
Show the current cursor position as
.IR x,y .
.SS monitors
.TP
.B monitors
List connected outputs (shorthand for
.BR "get monitors" ).
.SS reload
.TP
.B reload
Reload
.I config.toml
and
.IR theme.toml .
Equivalent to sending
.BR SIGUSR1 .
.SS plugin
.TP
.B plugin list
List all currently loaded plugins.
.TP
.BI plugin " load " path
Load the plugin at \fIpath\fR (a compiled \fB.so\fR). Emits
.B plugin_loaded
or
.B plugin_error
IPC event.
.TP
.BI plugin " unload " name
Unload the plugin with the given name.
.SS shader
.TP
.BI shader " set " "\-\-window " id " " path
Assign a per-window GLSL fragment shader.
.TP
.BI shader " screen " path
Set the global screen post-process shader.
.TP
.B shader clear
Remove the active screen shader.
.SS setprop
.TP
.BI setprop " id prop value"
Set a per-window property at runtime.
.PP
.B Supported properties:
.IR is_urgent ", " sticky ", " pin ", " no_animations ", " steal_focus ", "
.IR above_total_fullscreen ", " opacity " (0.0\(en1.0), "
.IR border_color " (hex string), " shader " (path or empty to clear)."
.SS kill
.TP
.B kill
Ask the compositor to exit cleanly.
.SS subscribe
.TP
.B subscribe [\fIevent\fR...]
Subscribe to the event socket and print events as they arrive.
Optionally filter to specific event names.
Events are emitted one per line in the format
.IR "name>>data" .
.PP
.B Available events:
workspace_changed, window_opened, window_closed, window_focus,
submap_changed, config_reloaded, config_error, overview_opened,
overview_closed, view_mode_changed, plugin_loaded, plugin_error.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
When
.B \-j
is given (or an endpoint is prefixed with
.BR j/ ),
all responses are JSON.
Structured responses use arrays of objects with camelCase keys.
.SH BATCH MODE
.PP
.RS
.EX
griddyctl \-\-batch "dispatch slot-half-left ; dispatch focus-right"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Commands are executed in order; responses are separated by
.BR "\\x04"
(EOT) on the socket and by newlines when printed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GRIDDY_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
Set by
.BR griddy (1)
to
.BI griddy_ PID\fR.
.B griddyctl
uses this to locate the runtime socket directory.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Socket files are placed in
.IB $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR / griddy_PID /
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/griddy_PID/griddy.sock
Command socket (request/response).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/griddy_PID/griddy-events.sock
Event socket (subscribe-only; events are one-way from compositor to client).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The compositor is not running or the socket is not reachable.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command or arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Switch to workspace at column 1, row 0:
.RS
.EX
griddyctl dispatch workspace 1,0
.EE
.RE
.PP
List all windows as JSON:
.RS
.EX
griddyctl \-j get windows
.EE
.RE
.PP
Tile focused window in the top-left quarter, then move focus right:
.RS
.EX
griddyctl \-\-batch "dispatch slot-quarter-tl ; dispatch focus-right"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Watch for workspace and focus changes:
.RS
.EX
griddyctl subscribe workspace_changed window_focus
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR griddy (1)
.SH AUTHORS
GriddyWM contributors.
